@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title claudecode paradigm — ML blackbox algorithm (spec → plan → implement → verify → loop)

actor "Developer\ngoal + stopping condition" as DEV

node "claudecode container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh" as EP <<app>>
  component "claude --dangerously-skip-permissions" as CLI <<error>>
  artifact "CLAUDE.md\nloop pattern + acceptance criteria" as MD <<db>>
  component "verification commands\n(internal/verify preamble)" as VER <<app>>
  database "/app (repo)\n/app/output (artifacts)" as WS <<db>>
  component "~/.claude/agents\narchitect · monorepo-coordinator\nadversarial-reviewer · security-reviewer\nspec-keeper" as SUB <<app>>
}

DEV ARROW_MAIN CLI : goal
EP ARROW_MAIN MD : seed when absent
EP ARROW_MAIN VER
EP ARROW_MAIN SUB : seed when absent\n(""CLAUDECODE_RESEED=1"" refreshes)
EP ARROW_MAIN CLI : " ""ANTHROPIC_MODEL"" \n""ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL"" (bare ids) "
CLI ARROW_OPTIONAL SUB : design before code · review the diff
SUB ARROW_ERROR CLI : ""[BLOCKER]"" / ""[HIGH]"" blocks completion
SUB ARROW_MAIN WS : spec-keeper only\n(""_spec/"" · ""PLAN.md"" · ""CLAUDE.md"")
CLI ARROW_MAIN WS : implement
CLI ARROW_MAIN VER : verify
VER ARROW_MAIN CLI : loop until acceptance criteria met
CLI ARROW_MAIN DEV : stops on the stated condition

note right of CLI
  **The dangerous flag is deliberate** — and is only
  acceptable because containment is external: hardened
  container + enforced egress + credential broker
  (_spec/_paradigms/egress-boundary.puml,
   _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml).
  Nothing here relies on the model's restraint.

  Small verifiable loops beat large open-ended tasks;
  errors are expected — the value is fast iteration
  inside the loop.
end note

note left of SUB
  **Read-only by allowlist, not by prose.** Under
  ""--dangerously-skip-permissions"" a reviewer that could
  edit could fix its own findings and mark itself green,
  so every advisor's frontmatter ""tools:"" is
  ""Read, Grep, Glob"" — no ""Edit"", no ""Write"", no ""Bash""
  for anyone. The lead runs ""git diff"" and hands it over.

  ""spec-keeper"" is the single writer, scoped by its prompt
  to ""_spec/"", ""PLAN.md"", ""CLAUDE.md"", ""AGENTS.md"".

  The definitions alone are inert — ""CLAUDE.md"" steps 3, 6
  and 7 are what make a subagent run.
end note

note bottom of WS
  ""layout: app"" — the only harness that does not
  use ""/app"". ""/workspace"" itself is **not** a mount, so a
  path outside ""input""/""output"" is written into the
  container's ephemeral layer and lost on exit.
end note

note bottom of EP
  Variants share this paradigm: ""mcp"" is the **default**
  image (""proveo/claudecode""); ""solidity"" layers the EVM
  contract toolchain (Foundry · solc · solhint · semgrep)
  **on top of mcp** — the heaviest variant; ""-browser"" is
  mcp FROM base-node-browser (Playwright + Chromium).

  Subscription harness: proveo warns rather than prompts
  when ""CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN"" is absent and lets the
  agent handle login.
end note

note right of CLI
  **No DinD.** Alone in the fleet, claudecode ships no
  docker client and stays ""dind: false"": the privileged
  sibling is ""broker""-mode only, and this is the harness
  whose permission posture depends on the boundary that
  mode removes. Container work stays deferred to the
  per-sandbox engine in
  _spec/_experiments/docker-sandbox.puml
  (Cursor-led experiment; claudecode is secondary).
end note
note bottom of CLI
  **""--verbose"" is the switch that shows full tool inputs and outputs**
  instead of collapsed one-line summaries, and it is also what the CLI
  requires before it will stream events in print mode.

  ""--debug"" is deliberately NOT added: it logs transport — MCP handshakes,
  API retries, startup — which is noise about the plumbing rather than
  evidence of the agent's work.

  A caller that already asked for ""stream-json"" also gets
  ""--include-partial-messages"", where the reasoning deltas live. A plain
  ""-p"" is left alone: changing a script's output format would break its
  parser, and that contract is the caller's, not ours.
end note

note bottom of CLI
  **The classic renderer is part of agent evidence.**
  Fullscreen draws on the alternate screen and
  restores it on exit, so a finished — or failed —
  run leaves nothing in scrollback, nothing for the
  transcript's tee, and an empty pane for a probe.
end note

note bottom of CLI
  ""CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=0"" is the documented off
  switch and out-ranks a saved ""tui"" setting, so a
  mounted home carrying ""fullscreen"" cannot re-enter
  it. The entrypoint defaults it; an operator who
  exports their own value keeps it.
end note

@enduml
